          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 1,
          "question": {
            "text": "Which one of the following is correct order of given isotopes?\r\nI. $T_2>D_2>P_2$ (order of boiling point)\r\nII. $T_2>D_2>P_2$ (order of bond energy)\r\nIII. $T_2=D_2=P_2$ (order of bond length)\r\nIV. $T_2 < D_2 < P_2$ (order of reactivity with $\\mathrm{Cl}_2$ )",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "pKKgJ",
              "text": "\r\nI and II\r\n",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "ud8H2",
              "text": "\r\nIII and IV\r\n",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "x1nfn",
              "text": "\r\nII, III and IV\r\n",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "M35Ny",
              "text": "\r\nAll of these",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Protium $(P)$, deuterium $(D)$ and tritium $(T)$ are the three isotopes of hydrogen. These isotopes follow the order in different contexts as shown below :\r\n$T_2>D_2>P_2$ [Order of boiling point (BP)]\r\n$T_2>D_2>P_2$ [Order of bond energy $\\left.(\\mathrm{BE})\\right]$\r\n$T_2=D_2=P_2$ [Order of bond length $\\left.(\\mathrm{BL})\\right]$\r\n$T_2 < D_2 < P_2$ [Order of reactivity with $\\mathrm{Cl}_2$ ]\r\nHence, all the given order are correct.",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
